# Sonoff Dual R2 blinds controller

Arduino firmware for a Sonoff Dual R2 used as a motorized blinds controller.

The firmware opts into the IoTCloud offline recovery watchdog. If full WiFi/MQTT
connectivity remains unavailable continuously for 15 minutes, the device
restarts so a wedged ESP8266 radio can recover. Other IoTCloud devices remain
unaffected unless they explicitly opt in.

## GPIO mapping

Use raw ESP8266 GPIO numbers, not board `D*` aliases:

| Component | GPIO |
| --- | --- |
| Relay A / UP | 12 |
| Relay B / DOWN | 5 |
| Blue status LED | 13 |
| Case button | 10 |

## MQTT commands

The sensor listens on:

`{mqtt_header}{sensor_id}/aux/setMovement`

Accepted payloads are signed numeric percentages from `-100` to `100`:

- Positive values open/up.
- Negative values close/down.
- `0` stops.
- Decimals are accepted, for example `12.5`.

Examples:

- `100` opens for the fixed full-open command time.
- `25` opens for 25% of the full open time.
- `-12.5` closes for 12.5% of the full close time.
- `-100` closes for the full close time.
- `0` stops.

Finite out-of-range values are clamped to `-100` or `100`. Malformed and
non-finite payloads are ignored. Non-zero commands whose computed duration is
below 250 ms are ignored.

Any movement command received while the blinds are already moving stops the
blinds. It does not reverse direction.

Reversing always leaves both relays off for at least 500 ms: a command in the
opposite direction sent right after a stop starts once that time has passed.
A command received during that wait cancels it.

The firmware publishes retained movement status on:

`{mqtt_header}{sensor_id}/aux/movement`

Possible movement payloads are `opening`, `closing`, and `stopped`.

## Settings

The full travel time is configurable through:

- `aux/fullOpenTime`
- `aux/fullCloseTime`
- `aux/fullOpenCommandTime`
- `aux/disableStatusLed`

Default timings:

| Setting | Default |
| --- | ---: |
| `fullOpenTime` | 16667 |
| `fullCloseTime` | 18333 |
| `fullOpenCommandTime` | 23500 |

Timing updates must be complete integer payloads between `1000` and `60000`
milliseconds. Malformed and out-of-range values are ignored.

`disableStatusLed` defaults to `false`. Publish `true` to keep the blue LED off.
